<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Backup rules for Android 11 and below (API 30-). API 31+ uses data_extraction_rules.xml.

    This file used to be the commented-out template, which meant "everything in the app's data
    directory leaves the device" was the default rather than a decision. It is now a decision.

    What the app stores is one SharedPreferences file, localuno_prefs: a display name, an avatar
    colour index, games played and won, two skin preferences, and a random per-device UUID used as
    the player id. Nothing secret, nothing about anyone else, and no table PIN - a PIN lives only in
    the hosting screen's state for the life of that lobby and is never written to disk.

    So backup stays ON: restoring your name, your stats and your identity onto a new phone is a
    small kindness and costs nothing. The rule is explicit rather than implicit so that if anything
    sensitive is ever added to these preferences, whoever adds it has to come here and say so.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <include domain="sharedpref" path="localuno_prefs.xml" />
</full-backup-content>
